# __APP_NAME__

A [RayX](https://github.com/rayx-ui/RayX) app on [NSH](https://github.com/dXnSix/nsh), made by
`rayx new`. __TEMPLATE__

- `Cargo.toml` depends on `rayx` at the tag of the `rayx` that made the app (`__RAYX_TAG__`);
  `.cargo/config.toml` patches NSH to the fork tag that RayX release builds with, and `Cargo.lock`
  records its commit, which is the nsh every `rayx app` command runs. Move them together: a newer
  `rayx` tag with that release's NSH patch.
- `src/lib.rs` names the app's services (`fn app`): RayX's are listed in its `docs/services.md`.

```sh
rayx app run                      # this machine's backend; --target ios, android, web, macos, linux, windows
rayx app check                    # cargo check of the crate, then the type checks
rayx app test                     # cargo test, then App.test.tsx, headless
rayx app package --target web     # or ios, android, macos, linux, windows
```

`rayx app` runs nsh's own commands with the nsh the app pins, installing it and what the target
needs first; `rayx doctor` shows the pins and what is missing.
